(#§ The round's solutions, which differ from its problems in two words, one file name and the
   line that follows each title: who wrote the solution and who marked it, where the problems
   booklet says what the problem is worth. §#)
(@§ extends 'round-base.jtyp' §@)
(@§ set kind = 'solution' §@)
(@§ set kind_verbose = 'Riešenia' §@)

(#§ `credits.credits`. The names go bold as one span rather than one each: `format_people`
   emits the joined list and `textbf` is LaTeX, so wrapping each name would mean a Typst
   `strong` in `StaticRenderer`'s vocabulary, which is documented and tested per name. §#)
(@§ block heading_inner §@)
(@§- if problem.solution -§@)
vzorák *(* problem.solution|format_people *)*
(@§- endif -§@)
(@§- if problem.evaluation -§@)
, opravoval(* problem.evaluation|format_gender_suffix *) *(* problem.evaluation|format_people *)*
(@§- endif -§@)
(@§ endblock §@)
